meta {
  name: Pair Initiate
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/auth/pair/initiate
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  Start a device pairing window. The 8-digit pairing code is printed only to
  the SERVER TERMINAL — never returned in the API response — so completing the
  pairing requires physical (or terminal) access to the host.

  Response:
    200 { "message": "...", "expires_at": <unix-secs> }
    409 ALREADY_EXISTS  → an unexpired pairing window is already active.
                         Wait for it to expire or finish that one first.

  Notes:
    - Window TTL: 5 minutes (configurable via `auth.pairing_code_ttl_secs`).
    - This endpoint is rate-limited per IP together with /auth/pair/complete,
      /auth/login, /auth/refresh: burst 5, replenish ~1/12s. Exceeding the
      bucket returns 429 (plain text from tower_governor).
    - Workflow:
        1. POST /auth/pair/initiate
        2. Read the 8-digit code printed in the server terminal
        3. POST /auth/pair/complete with the code (within 5 min)
}
